    <p>The Site is provided on an “as available” basis. We may update, suspend, or remove pages or features. We do not promise uninterrupted access, a particular response time, or that every example matches your environment.</p>
    <h2 id="software">3. Software and open-source licenses</h2>
    <p>Source code and software are governed by the license included with the relevant repository or release. These Site terms do not replace or expand that license. Product names, logos, and third-party marks remain with their respective owners. You are responsible for reviewing dependencies and license notices before use.</p>
    <h2 id="acceptable-use">4. Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>Use the Site and any tools only for lawful purposes and on repositories or systems you own or are authorized to assess. Do not attempt to disrupt the Site, bypass access controls, upload harmful material, misrepresent a scan, or use the content to make a safety decision without appropriate human review. See the <a href="/acceptable-use/">Acceptable Use Policy</a> for further guidance.</p>
    <h2 id="contact">5. Contact and form submissions</h2>
    <p>Forms on this static Site create an email draft in your browser; they do not submit information to a Neukee form server. You decide whether to send that email. Do not include passwords, private keys, production secrets, customer records, or source code you are not permitted to disclose. See the <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Notice</a> for details about the website host, font requests, and email.</p>
    <h2 id="third-parties">6. Third-party sites</h2>
    <p>Links to GitHub, release notes, scheduling tools, and other services are provided for convenience. Those services have their own operators, terms, and privacy practices. We do not control or endorse every statement, product, or change made on an external site.</p>
    <h2 id="warranties">7. Disclaimers</h2>
    <p>To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, the Site and its content are provided without warranties of any kind, express or implied. We do not warrant that examples are complete, that a tool is fit for a particular purpose, or that a reported issue is exhaustive. Nothing in these terms removes rights that cannot legally be excluded.</p>
    <h2 id="liability">8. Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>To the maximum extent permitted by law, the Site publisher is not liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive loss arising from use of the Site or reliance on its content. This does not exclude liability that cannot lawfully be limited, including liability for fraud or intentional misconduct where applicable.</p>
    <h2 id="changes">9. Changes</h2>
    <p>We may revise these terms as the Site changes. The “Last updated” date identifies the current version. Continued use after an update means the revised terms apply to future Site use, subject to mandatory legal rights.</p>
